{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1302365-do-you-ever-buy-melee-as-a-mage","id":1302365,"title":"Do you ever buy melee as a mage?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-04-03T16:14:25-07:00","id":1302365,"title":"Do you ever buy melee as a mage?","content":"Unlike Vampires, Mages have a lot of ways to deal aggravated damage, including in close combat. Using Forces, Prime or even Life to make unnarmed attacks somehow deal aggravated damage is possible and probably a better option. Avoiding carrying a melee weapon, such as a sword or a knife might be a good idea in a world where you don't want to draw attention or get in trouble.<br /> Even some martial arts attacks using Martial Arts or Do, can deal lethal damage.<br /> <br /> So, besides the cool factor, and the bonus damage in case of big swords or axes, there is any reason for a Mage to buy melee skill points?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-03T16:25:42-07:00","id":1302368,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1302365-do-you-ever-buy-melee-as-a-mage#post1302365\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unlike Vampires, Mages have a lot of ways to deal aggravated damage, including in close combat. Using Forces, Prime or even Life to make unnarmed attacks somehow deal aggravated damage is possible and probably a better option. Avoiding carrying a melee weapon, such as a sword or a knife might be a good idea in a world where you don't want to draw attention or get in trouble.<br /> Even some martial arts attacks using Martial Arts or Do, can deal lethal damage.<br /> <br /> So, besides the cool factor, and the bonus damage in case of big swords or axes, there is any reason for a Mage to buy melee skill points?</div> </div> </div> </div>The capacity of a mage to make frighteningly effective improvised weapons is not to be underestimated.. whether its doing Str+5 agg with an appropriately attuned Ladder or transforming a flashlight into a lightsaber. This is of course not counting correspondence tricks that let you hide weapons wherever. Also you can parry stuff.. and you probably can't run around with Primum hands...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-03T16:39:31-07:00","id":1302372,"title":"","content":"Skipping the &quot;cool&quot; factor is not something to do lightly with Mage, since that matters a lot to Focus; esp. Instruments.<br /> <br /> Mages also don't have that many ways to deal Agg for the WoD. Vampires can all do Agg with bites, and there's multiple Disciplines that allow it as well. Garou can claw and bite for Agg depending on form.<br /> <br /> Mages can use Prime to enchant their attacks, or use Life 3. Unlike the others though, they get to pick their attack style rather than have to go with what their powers say (normally Brawl). Prime can enchant weapons too after all.<br /> <br /> Access to the parry maneuver and the extra damage is good. Potentially being able to claim a reach bonus esp. vs. unarmed opponents. Magic can conceal weapons from mundane attention with relative ease. And then there's a really important big reason: Wonders. While you can theoretically turn your hands into a Wonder too, that's a pretty hefty commitment. I can have a magical sword for killing, a magical stick for knocking people out, etc. While hardly a starting level thing, and not a huge edge, it's still worth considering the ease of diversity with tools compared to just using your body.<br /> <br /> So, yeah, my mages use Melee plenty. Though a lot of my more combative mages have a mix of relevant Abilities because 2-3 in the Ability + good Dex + magic lets them easily adapt to the situation at hand.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-03T19:20:33-07:00","id":1302419,"title":"","content":"It depends on the character/concept, but it's never been that uncommon for me. Obviously, some groups - Akashic, Chorus, Hermetics, Knights Templar, Wu Lung, Bata'a - are going to be more likely to have it than others - Sons of Ether, Virtual Adepts, Sisters of Hippolyta.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-04T01:01:03-07:00","id":1302498,"title":"","content":"Remember that Do turns all melee weapons (and any object that could be used as a melee weapon) into something much more effective.<br /> <br /> If you take Weapon Mastery, then for every dot in Melee you have you add a familiar weapon type to your list. As long as you're using one of those weapons you are at -1 difficulty. Furthermore, 10,000 weapons turns random objects into Bashing Weapons, Bashing Weapons into Lethal Weapons and gives Lethal Weapons + 1 damage.<br /> <br /> Weapon Mastery also applies to other weapon skills, like Athletics (Throwing), Archery, just not firearms. It does have this annoying downside where you only get the benefit if your Dex + Do is equal to or greater than your rating in Dex + Melee/etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-04T02:22:00-07:00","id":1302505,"title":"","content":"Also worth remembering is the optional weapon length rule:<br /> If you fight unarmed, or with a shorter melee weapon against somebody with a long Melee Weapon, you get one die subtracted from your attack roll. Hence it's not good to do plain brawling against a melee guy.<br /> <br /> And even WORSE (or better, if you are the one holding the melee weapon):<br /> If you attack somebody with unarmed attacks, and they have a sharp melee weapon they are parrying with, you automatically get hit with a 'rebound' attack if the parry was successful - the parrying guy reflexively rolls dex+melee, and if the parry was better than the unarmed attack you add one automatic success for every success the parry was better.<br /> TL;DR: Melee parry vs. unarmed attacks can *seriously* hurt the brawler.<br /> <br /> So, yeah. A Mage might want to use that to their advantage (or avoid running bare-knuckle into a fight like that), and then add magick on top.<br /> <br /> <br /> EDIT:<br /> Oh man, that also gave me an evil idea. Dodging only works if you have enough space to do so - else you can only Parry. And brawlers usually *can't* parry lethal melee weapons.<br /> Ergo, you use Correspondence or Forces to put up invisible barriers to the sides or behind the brawler.<br /> They try to dodge, which surprisingly does not *work*, and then you just melee the crap out of them. They can't do anything against the incoming blows.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 04-04-2019, 05:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-06T11:59:12-07:00","id":1303148,"title":"","content":"You can dodge melee without much space, bob and waving or spinning is possible. No need to parry.<br /> <br /> The bonus damage and size difference is good.<br /> My point is that any bonus/buff spell you can do in a melee weapon you can do in your body to be used with brawl/martial arts","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-06T12:21:29-07:00","id":1303153,"title":"","content":"Right up until it comes to Wonders. Give your body magical upgrades has a lot more downsides than doing the same thing to your weapons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-06T13:51:35-07:00","id":1303171,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1302365-do-you-ever-buy-melee-as-a-mage?p=1303153#post1303153\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Right up until it comes to Wonders. Give your body magical upgrades has a lot more downsides than doing the same thing to your weapons.</div> </div> </div> </div>What kind of downsides?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-06T14:26:56-07:00","id":1303182,"title":"","content":"Perma-dox, genetic flaws, and the like depending on your methods.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-06T18:09:11-07:00","id":1303225,"title":"","content":"Simply due to raw numbers, a melee weapon deals more damage than bare-handed attacks (unless you have Do, of course, which not all characters can get). You have to use Life magick, or some other kind of effect, just to have a chance to do as much damage as many melee weapons do <i>without</i> magick. If you don't want to risk casting an Effect to make your attacks better, melee alone is just better, at as far as non-firearm/archery is concerned. Obviously ranged attacks are great in any case, though they have their own downsides (noise, concealment, local laws, ammunition, etc.).<br /> <br /> And if you CAN afford to pump your attacks with magick, that just makes the superiority of melee weapons compared to hand-to-hand all the more apparent. In the case of Prime, weapons (Prime 2) are easier to enchant than one's body (Prime 3 + Life 3), at least as far as M20 is concerned. Even if you waive the Life prerequisite, making your fists do Aggravated damage is harder (both on experience and in pulling it off) than using a weapon for the task.<br /> <br /> On another note, people tend to put more stock in the ability for weapons to deal damage and pull off other maneuvers (like blocking a bullet) than they believe in a fist's ability to do the same. As such, while martial artists have gone to great lengths to seed the popular consciousness with Mythic Threads amenable to bare-handed feats (like breaking boards or even cinder blocks), people will still &quot;buy&quot; that a weapon can do these things easier. Ergo, while a Brawl/Martial Arts/Do focused Effect <i>might</i> be Coincidental, a Melee focused Effect is a surer bet. Making Effects less likely to attract Paradox is its own reward.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-06T23:34:44-07:00","id":1303256,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1302365-do-you-ever-buy-melee-as-a-mage?p=1303148#post1303148\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can dodge melee without much space, bob and waving or spinning is possible. No need to parry.</div> </div> </div> </div>This accounts for long stabbing motions, really. Not so much a wide swing of a large weapon, nor somebody getting very close with a knife. (Though the latter is simulated by a certain Dirty Fighting technique roll, which one needs to use for that case)<br /> <br /> That and while the rules acknowledge bobbing and weaving, they also say &quot;Dodging requires a certain amount of room to move. If you\u2019re in a tight doorway, it\u2019s pretty hard to dodge.&quot;<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-07T07:25:53-07:00","id":1303317,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1302365-do-you-ever-buy-melee-as-a-mage?p=1303256#post1303256\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This accounts for long stabbing motions, really. Not so much a wide swing of a large weapon, nor somebody getting very close with a knife. (Though the latter is simulated by a certain Dirty Fighting technique roll, which one needs to use for that case)<br /> <br /> That and while the rules acknowledge bobbing and weaving, they also say &quot;Dodging requires a certain amount of room to move. If you\u2019re in a tight doorway, it\u2019s pretty hard to dodge.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem is circumvented by practitioners of Do; one of the innate benefits is that you can &quot;parry&quot; all sorts of melee/close-range attacks with your own body. So while the invisible barriers trapping someone so that you can stab them or force them to take damage through parrying plan is very effective, in a tiny minority of cases you'll face an Akashayana who simply isn't bothered by having to deflect/absorb blows with their arms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-07T09:40:18-07:00","id":1303340,"title":"","content":"But the point is about dodging, which everyone can do, not Do, which is a secret practice of one of the Traditions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-07T11:30:24-07:00","id":1303370,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1302365-do-you-ever-buy-melee-as-a-mage?p=1303256#post1303256\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This accounts for long stabbing motions, really. Not so much a wide swing of a large weapon, nor somebody getting very close with a knife. (Though the latter is simulated by a certain Dirty Fighting technique roll, which one needs to use for that case)<br /> <br /> That and while the rules acknowledge bobbing and weaving, they also say &amp;quot;Dodging requires a certain amount of room to move. If you\u2019re in a tight doorway, it\u2019s pretty hard to dodge.&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say that in a small area you can dodge at +1 diff (maybe +2). And not allowing dodge only if you're restrained.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-07T14:19:00-07:00","id":1303408,"title":"","content":"Even so, difficulty modifiers are a huge deal. You don't want to be dodging at difficulty 8 to avoid a Str + 4L base difficulty 6 weapon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-08T07:06:05-07:00","id":1303520,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1302365-do-you-ever-buy-melee-as-a-mage?p=1303148#post1303148\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can dodge melee without much space, bob and waving or spinning is possible. No need to parry.<br /> <br /> The bonus damage and size difference is good.<br /> My point is that any bonus/buff spell you can do in a melee weapon you can do in your body to be used with brawl/martial arts</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> ...this is true of all tools. Tools make things easier. Would your character learn to use a hammer or &quot;PUNCH NAILS&quot; because its more efficient use of his time?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-08T08:06:54-07:00","id":1303531,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1302365-do-you-ever-buy-melee-as-a-mage?p=1303520#post1303520\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ...this is true of all tools. Tools make things easier. Would your character learn to use a hammer or &quot;PUNCH NAILS&quot; because its more efficient use of his time?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's worth remembering that physical objects help avert Vulgarity and avoid paradox. It's weird if someone pulls out a katana in public and slices someone's arm off (horrifying even), but it's less weird than someone chopping off someone's arm with a karate chop. Weapons just make good excuses for swift death.<br /> <br /> Naturally the devoted martial artist will know at least a little bit of everything, to get a well-rounded approach to their preferred method. The expanded rules in M20 include this idea that you can roll Perception + Ability to tell what your opponent might do next, to get a bonus to your response (for example, the Soft Fist move where you redirect their attack back at them). Well, it's hard to predict what someone will do with a knife without Melee; Perception + Melee one turn, Dexterity + Do the next (with a difficulty reduction) and now their stab towards you ends up buried in their gut. Can't say it was entirely your fault either; they tried to stab you!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-09T06:15:00-07:00","id":1303764,"title":"","content":"Also it is just embarrasing to not have any melee when wielding your ritual stave, sword or dagger (all of which are fairly common).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-10T11:46:53-07:00","id":1304000,"title":"","content":"I believe one of my old Mage characters had like a single dot of Melee to reflect he'd probably been in plenty of poker games where a switchblade fight might result from a sore loser's accusations of cheating. It was more flavor than anything else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-11T01:20:02-07:00","id":1304125,"title":"","content":"To begin with Melee is very useful in Umbra, where many tech just doesn't work. melee is also great vs undead, demons and such who can close into melee Really quickly. I personally may take Melee, if playing combat mage, but generally prefer to take Dream for duels and planned raids.<br /> But, one shouldn't underestimate melee oriented combat mage. If you stack points cleverly, you can get a fighting monster in very short order that could go toe-to-toe with nearly anything. So if you want a frontline fighter don't forget to take Niphilim and Genemods (mostly dexterity), as well as Life 3 and Spirit 3 with spirit 4 specialized foci for making Fetishes. And don't forget at least Blatancy 3.<br /> In very short order you mage can pump out awakened weapons and armor that soaks/deal aggreviated and is better then mundane, alongside an array of battle drugs, talens (for extra actions and buffs) and a pack of possessed dogs for support. Most effects with appropriate props would be very coincidental, but still enough to turn whole groups into kabab with preparation.<br /> I would also recommend to create Mask of The Wyrm, that has -4 dice terror on any melee enemy that sees it, and a few awakened smoke granades ($20 sold freely). You can also place a pact with some war/predatory spirit for max hax. and that with starting character no more then a week in game time. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1302365-do-you-ever-buy-melee-as-a-mage?p=1303317#post1303317\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem is circumvented by practitioners of Do; one of the innate benefits is that you can &quot;parry&quot; all sorts of melee/close-range attacks with your own body. So while the invisible barriers trapping someone so that you can stab them or force them to take damage through parrying plan is very effective, in a tiny minority of cases you'll face an Akashayana who simply isn't bothered by having to deflect/absorb blows with their arms.</div> </div> </div> </div>they can block aggreviated damage like that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4340,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","user":"Warpwind","date":". 04-11-2019, 04:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","name":"Warpwind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-11T02:24:22-07:00","id":1304133,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Warpwind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1302365-do-you-ever-buy-melee-as-a-mage?p=1304125#post1304125\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">they can block aggreviated damage like that?</div> </div> </div> </div>They cannot *soak* the damage, but the text says that they can parry Lethal brawl/melee attacks, which is the same as a dodge roll essentially, just using Dexterity + Brawl/MA/Do instead of Athletics.<br /> <br /> The text specifically says Lethal however, so if the weapon does Aggravated damage then I assume the block won't work at all, unless they've taken steps with Life or Prime to allow their body to handle the strain of deflecting such blows with the maneuver.<br /> <br /> Furthermore, the block/parry maneuver is a standard one (although it's limited to blocking bashing damage normally), so the Well Trained Advantage should kick in and lower the difficulty by 1, which is helpful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","user":"twig","date":". 04-11-2019, 05:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-11T07:55:38-07:00","id":1304192,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Warpwind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1302365-do-you-ever-buy-melee-as-a-mage?p=1304125#post1304125\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To begin with Melee is very useful in Umbra, where many tech just doesn't work. melee is also great vs undead, demons and such who can close into melee Really quickly.</div> </div> </div> </div>That and, in the case of vampires (and realistically all kinds of undead), normal ranged weapons deal bashing damage - and Vamps at least, after soak, half the bashing that makes it past that soak automagically. You deal your lucky, MASSIVE 8 successes bashing damage, the vamp soaks 3, and after halving you are left with....3 that make it through. And that was a really good hit.<br /> <br /> Bladed lethal melee weapons are actually the *best* mundane weapon against them - save for stuff like flamethrowers, Dragonsbreath shells or generally aimed shots to the head (which is an optional rule, if I recall right).<br /> And carrying firearms can, depending on character and location, be...troublesome. Carrying a good knife and knowing how to use it on the other hand...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 04-11-2019, 10:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-11T08:12:35-07:00","id":1304196,"title":"","content":"And to top it all off, guns need ammunition, and make a lot of noise. They're also incredibly expensive and heavily regulated.<br /> <br /> A knife is reliable, at the end of the day.<br /> <br /> Melee weapons have advantages over Brawl (parrying, Lethal damage without magick, easier/safer to enchant a knife permanently compared with your own pattern, weapon length advantage, relatively coincidental source of killing vs a punch), and advantages over Firearms (issues with undead, regulation, cost, maintenance, ammo), but they do also have their own problems.<br /> <br /> In an ideal world, a character would master a mixture of close range combat (Do and MA), long range combat (crossbows are ideal, and fit into traditional paradigms, plus they're silent and lethal, with their ammo being replaced more easily than bullets with Crafts or Matter), and weapon use (weapons that fit into Do practice).<br /> <br /> With the crossbow (Archery skill) and various MA weapons (Melee), they'll get -1 difficulty if you increase your Do high enough, and you can learn a Do technique that gives them an extra die of damage, which is neat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","user":"twig","date":". 04-11-2019, 11:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-11T10:11:34-07:00","id":1304229,"title":"","content":"Crossbows are in no way silent. Quieter than a gun yes, but still not silent.<br /> <br /> In addition Melee weapons are also under regulation and *You are a wizard.* Regulation means nothing to you.<br /> <br /> In an ideal world you have a correspondence ban that causes people to be incapable of touching you, and then a staff that shoots lightning and stores paradox.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-11T10:52:58-07:00","id":1304249,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1302365-do-you-ever-buy-melee-as-a-mage?p=1304229#post1304229\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In addition Melee weapons are also under regulation and *You are a wizard.* Regulation means nothing to you.</div> </div> </div> </div>Blades are under way, way less regulation than guns, usually. Even a smallish knife can help a lot.<br /> Also, saying that regulations mean nothing to Mages is...quite broad strokes for a couple of reasons, in my opinion.<br /> <br /> For one, just because you are a Mage does not mean that you suddenly stop believing in sleeper or community laws. You don't just stop having morals or..well...let go of everything you were before. Be it having a job, friends or your actual family. Even if the Mage cares less about the law, it might even simply boil down to the Mage not wanting folks they *know* finding out that they have a gun in their possession because of a certain stigma of having one, depending on the social circles (and state/country/whatever).<br /> <br /> Of all the WoD splats, Mages and Sorcerors are (at least for the most part) the most human after all.<br /> Naturally there are Mages who are on the opposite end that are more alien and creaturesque than most other beings you can meet, but the point generally still stands.<br /> <br /> The other half of the equiation is, of course, that just because you are a Mage does not mean your way of doing Magick, your teachings or your paradigm allow you to just hide things on your body, making things invisible, warding from touch or pull a &quot;These are not the droids you are looking for&quot; with the snap of a finger. It boils down to paradigm as usual, and I figure that it's *especially* the Mages that are not well versed in protection or magickal combat are those that benefit most from a mundane weapon just-in-case.<br /> <br /> While I get the gist of what you are saying, it's..as I said, *really* too broad to make it a definitive statement rather than a simple possibility.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 04-11-2019, 02:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-11T11:41:22-07:00","id":1304272,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1302365-do-you-ever-buy-melee-as-a-mage?p=1304229#post1304229\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Crossbows are in no way silent. Quieter than a gun yes, but still not silent.<br /> <br /> In addition Melee weapons are also under regulation and *You are a wizard.* Regulation means nothing to you.<br /> <br /> In an ideal world you have a correspondence ban that causes people to be incapable of touching you, and then a staff that shoots lightning and stores paradox.</div> </div> </div> </div>- Silent in the sense that a baseball bat, or any weapon, is silent. Any means of attacking someone has the potential to create some noise. Far quieter than even the most suppressed gunshot. The only significant noise will be the target shouting/screaming if they aren't killed immediately (which is what Magick helps with really; extra damage, better targeting of vital organs etc.)<br /> <br /> - Regulations mean a lot to Mages. Lots of Mages (perhaps even most) rely upon jobs, neighbors, friends. Carrying a gun around with you is a big deal, especially if you aren't doing it legally. They're difficult to hide and incredibly dangerous. Unless you intend to teleport away from every single police officer who asks to search your vehicle (hello Paradox, hello NWO, hello APB for a guy who resisted arrest), being a law-abiding citizen is quite important. And if you don't follow regulations, there are Mages who specialize in exploiting that to absolutely destroy you. Sure, a Syndicate rep absolutely couldn't beat you in a one-on-one fight... but your (business/home/vehicle) is nowhere NEAR matching code (didn't get your MOT, didn't file your tax properly, didn't make contributions into employee's pensions, didn't make things accessible to disabled clientele, vehicle is dangerous and you're using it to transport others), and with the right effects that can completely ruin your life financially and legally. Even without the interference of hypereconomists and magickal bureaucrats, there's still the fact that living in a society demands following its rules, for a Mage to escape those rules they need to use magick, and using magick constantly to evade these rules will attract both Paradox and negative consequences.<br /> <br /> Knives are easier to conceal (smaller, less heavy), and it's less abnormal to carry them in almost any context. Still unacceptable in many situations, but there are always plausible excuses. It's for fishing, it's for hunting etc.<br /> <br /> - If the staff is storing paradox, then it's got a Periapt built into it. When (not if, since we're flinging around lightning to solve all our problems because We Are Mages I guess) it accumulates enough Paradox, it's gonna blow and you're going to have one hell of a backlash to deal with (even forgetting all the extra paradox you're probably carrying from creating Bans and various other forms of magick).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-11T18:21:55-07:00","id":1304365,"title":"","content":"Guys, I'm not comparing melee with firearm or bows/crossbows. I'm comparing using melee with magically enhanced martial arts/brawl to deal agg damage. But I got the point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-13T01:04:32-07:00","id":1304590,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1302365-do-you-ever-buy-melee-as-a-mage?p=1304229#post1304229\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Crossbows are in no way silent. Quieter than a gun yes, but still not silent.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would be more for high power bows, enhanced of course and blowpipes with magical darts.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In addition Melee weapons are also under regulation and *You are a wizard.* Regulation means nothing to you. </div> </div> </div>greatest supplies of melee weapons are found in hardware stores. really, if it isn't something very special you are better off carrying crowbar or ice pick then a zweihander. You could also take a solid steel staff and paint it to look like wood. <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In an ideal world you have a correspondence ban that causes people to be incapable of touching you, and then a staff that shoots lightning and stores paradox. </div> </div> </div>I prefer the one that makes attacks 'miss', way more surreptitious. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","name":"Warpwind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-14T04:24:57-07:00","id":1304778,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1302365-do-you-ever-buy-melee-as-a-mage?p=1304272#post1304272\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- Regulations mean a lot to Mages. Lots of Mages (perhaps even most) rely upon jobs, neighbors, friends. Carrying a gun around with you is a big deal, especially if you aren't doing it legally. They're difficult to hide and incredibly dangerous. Unless you intend to teleport away from every single police officer who asks to search your vehicle (hello Paradox, hello NWO, hello APB for a guy who resisted arrest), being a law-abiding citizen is quite important. And if you don't follow regulations, there are Mages who specialize in exploiting that to absolutely destroy you. Sure, a Syndicate rep absolutely couldn't beat you in a one-on-one fight... but your (business/home/vehicle) is nowhere NEAR matching code (didn't get your MOT, didn't file your tax properly, didn't make contributions into employee's pensions, didn't make things accessible to disabled clientele, vehicle is dangerous and you're using it to transport others), and with the right effects that can completely ruin your life financially and legally. Even without the interference of hypereconomists and magickal bureaucrats, there's still the fact that living in a society demands following its rules, for a Mage to escape those rules they need to use magick, and using magick constantly to evade these rules will attract both Paradox and negative consequences.</div> </div> </div> </div>All this assumes that the Mage starts on a good or neutral footing, in respect to the law. That the Mage doesn't already have a target painted on their back, as far as the powers-that-be are concerned.<br /> <br /> A not insignificant number of Mages have been institutionalized, at one point or another. Think the Dreamspeaker that got sent to a mental asylum for the &quot;voices in their head&quot;. The Children of Knowledge alchemist who got locked up in a previous life for cooking meth or other illicit substances. The Euthanatos killer who is wanted in eight states. The Orphan who lost their parents young (in an Awakening-induced disaster), and spent years in the foster system. An Ecstatic who had a stint in rehab. Even characters who were never IN an institution might have trouble with the law. Like any number of Mages who happen to control a Cult, which is or could be under the watchful eye of the authorities.<br /> <br /> Not to mention the clustercrap that arises from systemic prejudice. All because a Mage committed the &quot;crime&quot; of not being white, male, straight, or conforming to other social, behavioral, or religious norms. Minorities in our world get killed all the time by police, despite doing nothing illegal.<br /> <br /> None of these things make it any easier for the Mage, if she's caught carrying a gun. Someone who was a former mental patient or ex-con might have been stripped of their right to own guns. Under this or other conditions, the Mage can expect much worse treatment from authorities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-14T07:04:57-07:00","id":1304803,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1302365-do-you-ever-buy-melee-as-a-mage?p=1304778#post1304778\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> All this assumes that the Mage starts on a good or neutral footing, in respect to the law. That the Mage doesn't already have a target painted on their back, as far as the powers-that-be are concerned.<br /> <br /> A not insignificant number of Mages have been institutionalized, at one point or another. Think the Dreamspeaker that got sent to a mental asylum for the &quot;voices in their head&quot;. The Children of Knowledge alchemist who got locked up in a previous life for cooking meth or other illicit substances. The Euthanatos killer who is wanted in eight states. The Orphan who lost their parents young (in an Awakening-induced disaster), and spent years in the foster system. An Ecstatic who had a stint in rehab. Even characters who were never IN an institution might have trouble with the law. Like any number of Mages who happen to control a Cult, which is or could be under the watchful eye of the authorities.<br /> <br /> Not to mention the clustercrap that arises from systemic prejudice. All because a Mage committed the &quot;crime&quot; of not being white, male, straight, or conforming to other social, behavioral, or religious norms. Minorities in our world get killed all the time by police, despite doing nothing illegal.<br /> <br /> None of these things make it any easier for the Mage, if she's caught carrying a gun. Someone who was a former mental patient or ex-con might have been stripped of their right to own guns. Under this or other conditions, the Mage can expect much worse treatment from authorities.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, most people are (almost unavoidably) on the grid. That's why at my table, it's common practice in the traditions to try and &quot;obfuscate&quot; your past as you enter into your life as a mage. Take steps to cover your tracks where possible, take a new name, change your appearance. This is why mages tend to have enigmatic and cool names; a James Smith can become a Darius Doyle if they want to. Members of houses sometimes take their House as a new surname; Shaea Hermetics call eachother sister/brother/mother/father/etc. and have Shaea as their surname (since they know so well the power a name can hold).<br /> <br /> Virtual Adepts are, well, adept at destroying and changing records. The &quot;schizophrenic&quot; native boy (a Dreamspeaker who was institutionalized when he Awakened) who is in mental health records can be changed digitally so that the truth is covered up (hopefully) forever. This means that it will be more difficult for the NWO to find details of Traditions Mages.<br /> <br /> Anyways yeah the overall sense at my table is that the Traditions have a strong idea of what sort of things the Union can exploit, and Mages take steps to protect themselves where possible. And this is why the NWO still values physical records! Harder to alter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-15T16:19:15-07:00","id":1305160,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1302365-do-you-ever-buy-melee-as-a-mage?p=1304249#post1304249\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Blades are under way, way less regulation than guns, usually. Even a smallish knife can help a lot.<br /> Also, saying that regulations mean nothing to Mages is...quite broad strokes for a couple of reasons, in my opinion.<br /> <br /> For one, just because you are a Mage does not mean that you suddenly stop believing in sleeper or community laws. You don't just stop having morals or..well...let go of everything you were before. Be it having a job, friends or your actual family. Even if the Mage cares less about the law, it might even simply boil down to the Mage not wanting folks they *know* finding out that they have a gun in their possession because of a certain stigma of having one, depending on the social circles (and state/country/whatever).<br /> <br /> Of all the WoD splats, Mages and Sorcerors are (at least for the most part) the most human after all.<br /> Naturally there are Mages who are on the opposite end that are more alien and creaturesque than most other beings you can meet, but the point generally still stands.<br /> <br /> The other half of the equiation is, of course, that just because you are a Mage does not mean your way of doing Magick, your teachings or your paradigm allow you to just hide things on your body, making things invisible, warding from touch or pull a &quot;These are not the droids you are looking for&quot; with the snap of a finger. It boils down to paradigm as usual, and I figure that it's *especially* the Mages that are not well versed in protection or magickal combat are those that benefit most from a mundane weapon just-in-case.<br /> <br /> While I get the gist of what you are saying, it's..as I said, *really* too broad to make it a definitive statement rather than a simple possibility.</div> </div> </div> </div>A smallish knife, isn't going to help you in a swordfight. And actually, Blades might be easier to get ahold of, but people are going to STOP you if they see you with a blade in public. Guns are more effective and easier to hide than a blade that's good enough to actually help you.<br /> <br /> Personally, I see Mages as by default, Humanity 0. These are people so convinced of their own innate rightness that they warp reality to fit their vision. Most Mage groups have at least one or two genocides under their belt, and engage in behaviour that in other splats would have you rocketing downwards on the morality scale.<br /> <br /> They're not creaturesqe, and that's their unique horror. Mages are men and women, normal men and women, given the power to try and make the world what they think it should be, and the absolute belief in the righteousness of their own particular philosophy. Which makes them more terrifying monsters than literally any of the other lines by default.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1302365-do-you-ever-buy-melee-as-a-mage?p=1304272#post1304272\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> - Silent in the sense that a baseball bat, or any weapon, is silent. Any means of attacking someone has the potential to create some noise. Far quieter than even the most suppressed gunshot. The only significant noise will be the target shouting/screaming if they aren't killed immediately (which is what Magick helps with really; extra damage, better targeting of vital organs etc.)<br /> <br /> - Regulations mean a lot to Mages. Lots of Mages (perhaps even most) rely upon jobs, neighbors, friends. Carrying a gun around with you is a big deal, especially if you aren't doing it legally. They're difficult to hide and incredibly dangerous. Unless you intend to teleport away from every single police officer who asks to search your vehicle (hello Paradox, hello NWO, hello APB for a guy who resisted arrest), being a law-abiding citizen is quite important. And if you don't follow regulations, there are Mages who specialize in exploiting that to absolutely destroy you. Sure, a Syndicate rep absolutely couldn't beat you in a one-on-one fight... but your (business/home/vehicle) is nowhere NEAR matching code (didn't get your MOT, didn't file your tax properly, didn't make contributions into employee's pensions, didn't make things accessible to disabled clientele, vehicle is dangerous and you're using it to transport others), and with the right effects that can completely ruin your life financially and legally. Even without the interference of hypereconomists and magickal bureaucrats, there's still the fact that living in a society demands following its rules, for a Mage to escape those rules they need to use magick, and using magick constantly to evade these rules will attract both Paradox and negative consequences.<br /> <br /> Knives are easier to conceal (smaller, less heavy), and it's less abnormal to carry them in almost any context. Still unacceptable in many situations, but there are always plausible excuses. It's for fishing, it's for hunting etc.<br /> <br /> - If the staff is storing paradox, then it's got a Periapt built into it. When (not if, since we're flinging around lightning to solve all our problems because We Are Mages I guess) it accumulates enough Paradox, it's gonna blow and you're going to have one hell of a backlash to deal with (even forgetting all the extra paradox you're probably carrying from creating Bans and various other forms of magick).</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, by the same virtue, you could just use forces to cancel out the sound of the gunshot. That's what the Ultra-Silencer does in the Technocracy book. It's an artifact that cancels out all sound of the gunshot.<br /> <br /> Those mages are what we call 'Corpses'. Any Mage who's that enmeshed into a 'normal' life is already on a Technocracy hitlist and it's just a matter of convenience as to when you die. That's the thing. Mage isn't ABOUT being 'just a normal guy' You have an alternate worldview that looks at the modern world as something every bit as alien and foreign as the Technocracy views the Traditional paradigms.<br /> <br /> A knife that's useful in a fight is no easier to conceal than a pistol. And knives that would be used for fishing or hunting would be of the 'Your still doing unarmed strikes but they deal lethal damage now' variety. Trying to block a sword with a hunting knife? That's ridiculous.<br /> <br /> No, it's got a periapt ATTACHED to it. You take the Periapt off, and let it bleed off the paradox, and cycle it out with another one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-16T02:01:48-07:00","id":1305221,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1302365-do-you-ever-buy-melee-as-a-mage?p=1305160#post1305160\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally, I see Mages as by default, Humanity 0. These are people so convinced of their own innate rightness that they warp reality to fit their vision. Most Mage groups have at least one or two genocides under their belt, and engage in behaviour that in other splats would have you rocketing downwards on the morality scale.<br /> <br /> They're not creaturesqe, and that's their unique horror. Mages are men and women, normal men and women, given the power to try and make the world what they think it should be, and the absolute belief in the righteousness of their own particular philosophy. Which makes them more terrifying monsters than literally any of the other lines by default.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I very much agree with a lot of this <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> But I think it highly depends on the Mage in question, and also their age; That is, how long they have been awake.<br /> <br /> The state - heck, the actual moment of the event - of awakening fundamentally changes a person, at least when it comes to their very perceptions of the world.<br /> It can (and probably will) change more than just those over time, but the Mage also doesn't immediately drop all their morals, all their ingrained behaviors, social desires or relationships - the human psyche, even awakened, doesn't completely flip in an instant.<br /> <br /> In a way, where Vampire has the struggle between the vampire and their beast, where Werewolf has the struggle between a human or animal upbringing versus the strange new state of utter rage and gaian duty, Mage has its struggle between a simple human self, the awakened senses that are bound to change your mind, and the Avatar trying to steer and influence the Mage mentally and physically towards...well. The ways of the Avatar can be enigmatic.<br /> But strong Avatars certainy have a much bigger impact thank weak ones (Background-dot-wise, not actual Avatar-power-wise, given that the background even states that Avatar 1 can also mean a very powerful and ancient Avatar that is simply not very invested in you).<br /> It's why I see taking the Avatar background at 4-5 as quite a big deal for a character's RP.<br /> <br /> So yeah, every Mage turns at least a bit more alien compared to sleepers of course, but the degree varies on how much the Mage clings to what they have, on the influence of the Avatar, and the general mindset of the person in question.<br /> There are some that (mostly) manage to live a somewhat 'normal' life...heck, Destiny's Price is pretty much &quot;Struggles of Mages vs. Everyday Life - The Book&quot;.<br /> But many Mages depart from it, I agree; Both the Order Of Hermes as well as the Technocracy in general have their formal departure from their &quot;Oldlife&quot; for a reason - it makes this step easier in the way of making it mandatory, and then leaves it to the Mage to decide how much they want to interact with the Everyday.<br /> <br /> The other Traditions however do not really have such a formal departure, and here's where, I think, a lot of the Mages can be found that try to find a balance between the new and the old, or actually struggle more and more over time with keeping their old friends and assets - last but not least because they might lose the *desire* to do so.<br /> <br /> In the end the most frightening thing about Mages is, as you said - that they can look perfectly human, but mentally can be completely alien. And vice versa...you can have a Mage with an almost childlike joy of being able to change their body in downright bizarre ways, but fundamentally have a very relatable mind.<br /> With a Mage, you never know what you are looking at. You don't know how understandable or inhuman their logic or thoughts are, in their awakened state of dementia.<br /> <br /> Also, it's why <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/images/4261/162241.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/images/4261/162241.jpg</a> is one of my favorite depictions of a Mage. It's a wonderful example of one that is...very..eerie.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 04-16-2019, 03:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-16T04:47:01-07:00","id":1305236,"title":"","content":"Your perspective is...reversed?<br /> You ask why having melee when you can improvise weapons with magick.<br /> Yet, to many if not most mages, their magick to scramble someone's innards comes from using the weapon. Weapons are among the best metaphors possible for forcing your will upon something, and that'll tickle most mages' fancy.<br /> You also forget that many mages don't see much difference between mundane and magickal acts. And this means the mundane and magickal elements of their character <b>need</b> to converge.<br /> <br /> Some might also simply <i>not</i> have magick to do that stuff. Some might also have become competent weapon masters long before they awoke.<br /> <br /> Even from a &quot;optimizing the character sheet&quot; perspective you could have good reason to have melee. Blocks and attacks on the same ability? Why would I spend on both brawl and athletics?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-16T05:02:51-07:00","id":1305239,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1302365-do-you-ever-buy-melee-as-a-mage?p=1305160#post1305160\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, by the same virtue, you could just use forces to cancel out the sound of the gunshot. That's what the Ultra-Silencer does in the Technocracy book. It's an artifact that cancels out all sound of the gunshot.<br /> <br /> Those mages are what we call 'Corpses'. Any Mage who's that enmeshed into a 'normal' life is already on a Technocracy hitlist and it's just a matter of convenience as to when you die. That's the thing. Mage isn't ABOUT being 'just a normal guy' You have an alternate worldview that looks at the modern world as something every bit as alien and foreign as the Technocracy views the Traditional paradigms.<br /> <br /> A knife that's useful in a fight is no easier to conceal than a pistol. And knives that would be used for fishing or hunting would be of the 'Your still doing unarmed strikes but they deal lethal damage now' variety. Trying to block a sword with a hunting knife? That's ridiculous.<br /> <br /> No, it's got a periapt ATTACHED to it. You take the Periapt off, and let it bleed off the paradox, and cycle it out with another one.</div> </div> </div> </div>- Using Forces 2 to completely silence something means an Arete roll, and it's not always going to be Coincidental. Say it with me folks: Mages need to be able to do things without magick! Technically every ability could be substituted with magick, but doing that is a really bad idea. A weapon that doesn't need silencing with magick will trump a weapon that does.<br /> <br /> - That simply isn't true. Lots of Mages exist within the mundane world. The Technocracy doesn't have the resources to discover every single Mage in the population and kill them; otherwise the Pogrom would have wiped out the Traditions almost entirely (sparing the hermits and those who exist offworld). Simply put, Mages of all stripes exist in the normal world to a certain extent. They own businesses, they pay taxes, they rent, the rent out, they have neighbors, they have hobbies.<br /> <br /> That doesn't mean these mages are &quot;normal people&quot; but they do continue to exist in the normal world. The books are pretty clear on this; just look at the Backgrounds, the Social Merits, the rich descriptions of how Mages fit into communities and cities.They're <b><i>not</i></b> Ethereal Cosmic Occult Hobos (however that is a common trope in some Mage games; to avoid this one of the STs I know gives Resources 1 as a default, since he argues that it's basically impossible to exist without it, and having Resources 0 should make you the exception).<br /> <br /> Mages can, of course, become reclusive and shut themselves off from wider society. That's going to happen. Similar to Vampires and Werewolves they're going to become withdrawn and focus more and more on the &quot;secret life&quot; of the night-folk. But that isn't guaranteed to happen (the Crafts are absolutely invested into the communities from which they spring in many cases), and even if it does it doesn't mean you stop being part of society, you're simply a less active part of society. You go from being the friendly neighbor to being the reclusive odd neighbor. And that creates problems and drama.<br /> <br /> - Doing lethal damage is incredibly important, since humans can't soak it, and it takes ages to heal, meaning that your attacks are actually, well, lethal. Beating someone to death is HARD because you need to inflict 14 levels of damage to get the 7 lethal needed to kill them. Lethal vs Bashing damage is a CRITICAL distinction, arguably more important than Lethal vs Aggravated (the difference between Lethal and Aggravated is almost completely moot for mortals, who can't soak either, and heal them the same way).<br /> <br /> - Great, so add... Matter 5 to our list of Spheres We Just Happen to Have. Making several periapts and rotating them around... I mean yes it's effective, but I feel like we're brushing over just how powerful a Mage has to be to do this, and how much better it would be to solve these problems without vulgar/flashy magick where possible. Also throw in a Node, because why not. For what it's worth I house-rule periapts to not require Matter 5, making it a Matter/Prime deal, but we're talking RAW. And &quot;yeah using a knife to solve your problems without magick is something you could do, but what if you solved all of your problems with Level 5 Sphere effects and huge quantities of Quintessence instead&quot; feels like a... strange jump. Again, mundane solutions are something that Mages do rely upon, and relying entirely upon magickal solutions should be an in-universe character flaw. See the emphasis Mage places on abilities, on specialization, on the value of characters who are experts in mundane acts like hacking, car repair and singing. These abilities are the foundations of practice; if you can't solve mundane problems, you're probably going to struggle to solve problems mystically anyways.<br /> <br /> Part of the beauty of Mage is how the Mundane feeds into the Arcane. Having something simple/boring like Melee 2 can be the foundation of something really cool and special, like turning someone into Quintessence with a thrust of a sacrificial dagger.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","user":"twig","date":". 04-16-2019, 08:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-16T05:44:20-07:00","id":1305247,"title":"","content":"You can expect Melee mages to be scarce compared to, say, Firearms mages or Brawl mages, but that's far more a virtue of the modern world being more accomodating to the latter two than their Magick. Their Magick is actually likely to skew people towards using more Melee, compared to mundanes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":32,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","user":"Synapse","date":". 04-16-2019, 08:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-16T07:15:58-07:00","id":1305262,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Synapse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1302365-do-you-ever-buy-melee-as-a-mage?p=1305247#post1305247\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can expect Melee mages to be scarce compared to, say, Firearms mages or Brawl mages, but that's far more a virtue of the modern world being more accomodating to the latter two than their Magick. Their Magick is actually likely to skew people towards using more Melee, compared to mundanes.</div> </div> </div> </div>In a similar sense, Garou will be biased towards Brawl and Melee (claws and glaives), and Vampires will be biased towards Brawl and Melee (claws and fangs, the fact that swords&gt;bullets when fighting other vampires).<br /> <br /> The WoD has a Rule of Cool built into it that lets melee weapons function in the 21st century a bit better than they would otherwise, with a lot of details of supernatural beings having been arranged to allow this to work logically. WoD-Vampires and other undead are justified as being more vulnerable to cutting/slashing weapons than bullets since punctures mean little to them (they're not going to bleed out), but slicing through something will impair movement. WoD-Werewolves have powerful supernatural/ceremonial weapons. WoD-Mages have a much longer history of using melee weapons (across the Traditions and Crafts) than modern weapons, so knives and swords are more common in Hermetic Practice than firearms, plus ancient enchanted weapons are going to include spears and daggers but not machine guns (short of some very Mage-esque time-fuckery with people &quot;remembering&quot; how to make guns from the memories of their future lives).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","user":"twig","date":". 04-16-2019, 10:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-16T08:37:09-07:00","id":1305273,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1302365-do-you-ever-buy-melee-as-a-mage?p=1305262#post1305262\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In a similar sense, Garou will be biased towards Brawl and Melee (claws and glaives), and Vampires will be biased towards Brawl and Melee (claws and fangs, the fact that swords&gt;bullets when fighting other vampires).<br /> <br /> The WoD has a Rule of Cool built into it that lets melee weapons function in the 21st century a bit better than they would otherwise, with a lot of details of supernatural beings having been arranged to allow this to work logically. WoD-Vampires and other undead are justified as being more vulnerable to cutting/slashing weapons than bullets since punctures mean little to them (they're not going to bleed out), but slicing through something will impair movement. WoD-Werewolves have powerful supernatural/ceremonial weapons. WoD-Mages have a much longer history of using melee weapons (across the Traditions and Crafts) than modern weapons, so knives and swords are more common in Hermetic Practice than firearms, plus ancient enchanted weapons are going to include spears and daggers but not machine guns (short of some very Mage-esque time-fuckery with people &quot;remembering&quot; how to make guns from the memories of their future lives).</div> </div> </div> </div>Hell, in Mage, the Rule of Cool is a literal active force in-universe. That's what Mythic Threads are. At least in M20, a Mage adhering to what's <i>expected</i> of their magickal style can get reductions in difficulty, or even make Vulgar Effects Coincidental under the right circumstances.<br /> <br /> A Hermetic wizard in the modern day could wear sunglasses and a leather jacket, wielding a gun etched with Enochian script. There's even plenty of practical reasons to do so. But if the wizard stays true to their heritage, going Full Wizard - flowing robes, pointed hat, ornate staff, ritual dagger, etc - the Hermetic could get a boost to casting. While the Consensus in general prefers the modern and technological, it <i>remembers</i> the Old Ways. It <i>responds</i> to the Old Ways, even if it still treats them as Vulgar. The same general effect that allows unAwakened Sorcerers to cast spells in the old manner at all, also aids the Mage, to some degree.<br /> <br /> From that angle, wielding melee weapons in the modern day is a valid (albeit risky) choice, when it comes to channeling their classic Arts. It's not subtle, and guns beat all comers for a reason. But it's valid, if the Mage has the courage to embrace it.<br /> <br /> (This, incidentally, is one of the reasons I love M20. Much as I like the Gothic Punk of the 90s, players shouldn't be discouraged from playing to type.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-16T11:32:49-07:00","id":1305305,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't say the modern world is more Brawl friendly in some way. Basic self-defense classes are pretty common place, sure, but most of those include basic weapon use as well (even if 'more advanced' as a subject). Sport weapon fighting beyond fencing is making a comeback in the West and never went away in other parts of the world.<br /> <br /> And the simple fact of the matter is that while guns are more deadly than knives, Melee weapons are equally more deadly than fists. If anything, the game massively skews towards making Brawl more functional than it should be in comparison to Melee.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-16T11:49:38-07:00","id":1305308,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1302365-do-you-ever-buy-melee-as-a-mage?p=1305239#post1305239\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> - Using Forces 2 to completely silence something means an Arete roll, and it's not always going to be Coincidental. Say it with me folks: Mages need to be able to do things without magick! Technically every ability could be substituted with magick, but doing that is a really bad idea. A weapon that doesn't need silencing with magick will trump a weapon that does.<br /> <br /> - That simply isn't true. Lots of Mages exist within the mundane world. The Technocracy doesn't have the resources to discover every single Mage in the population and kill them; otherwise the Pogrom would have wiped out the Traditions almost entirely (sparing the hermits and those who exist offworld). Simply put, Mages of all stripes exist in the normal world to a certain extent. They own businesses, they pay taxes, they rent, the rent out, they have neighbors, they have hobbies.<br /> <br /> That doesn't mean these mages are &amp;quot;normal people&amp;quot; but they do continue to exist in the normal world. The books are pretty clear on this; just look at the Backgrounds, the Social Merits, the rich descriptions of how Mages fit into communities and cities.They're <b><i>not</i></b> Ethereal Cosmic Occult Hobos (however that is a common trope in some Mage games; to avoid this one of the STs I know gives Resources 1 as a default, since he argues that it's basically impossible to exist without it, and having Resources 0 should make you the exception).<br /> <br /> Mages can, of course, become reclusive and shut themselves off from wider society. That's going to happen. Similar to Vampires and Werewolves they're going to become withdrawn and focus more and more on the &amp;quot;secret life&amp;quot; of the night-folk. But that isn't guaranteed to happen (the Crafts are absolutely invested into the communities from which they spring in many cases), and even if it does it doesn't mean you stop being part of society, you're simply a less active part of society. You go from being the friendly neighbor to being the reclusive odd neighbor. And that creates problems and drama.<br /> <br /> - Doing lethal damage is incredibly important, since humans can't soak it, and it takes ages to heal, meaning that your attacks are actually, well, lethal. Beating someone to death is HARD because you need to inflict 14 levels of damage to get the 7 lethal needed to kill them. Lethal vs Bashing damage is a CRITICAL distinction, arguably more important than Lethal vs Aggravated (the difference between Lethal and Aggravated is almost completely moot for mortals, who can't soak either, and heal them the same way).<br /> <br /> - Great, so add... Matter 5 to our list of Spheres We Just Happen to Have. Making several periapts and rotating them around... I mean yes it's effective, but I feel like we're brushing over just how powerful a Mage has to be to do this, and how much better it would be to solve these problems without vulgar/flashy magick where possible. Also throw in a Node, because why not. For what it's worth I house-rule periapts to not require Matter 5, making it a Matter/Prime deal, but we're talking RAW. And &amp;quot;yeah using a knife to solve your problems without magick is something you could do, but what if you solved all of your problems with Level 5 Sphere effects and huge quantities of Quintessence instead&amp;quot; feels like a... strange jump. Again, mundane solutions are something that Mages do rely upon, and relying entirely upon magickal solutions should be an in-universe character flaw. See the emphasis Mage places on abilities, on specialization, on the value of characters who are experts in mundane acts like hacking, car repair and singing. These abilities are the foundations of practice; if you can't solve mundane problems, you're probably going to struggle to solve problems mystically anyways.<br /> <br /> Part of the beauty of Mage is how the Mundane feeds into the Arcane. Having something simple/boring like Melee 2 can be the foundation of something really cool and special, like turning someone into Quintessence with a thrust of a sacrificial dagger.</div> </div> </div> </div>- I mean, most guns are single shot and your mortal opponent is dead. If your opponent is tougher than that, you're better off fighting magic with magic. Also remember, Mages are squishy. Their entire skillset caters to incredibly destructive alpha strikes. Not toe to toe sword fights.<br /> <br /> - it takes prime 2 to deal aggravated damage with your fists. Do a small Kung Fu ritual before going out for a night of buttwooping. Your knife is now pointless.<br /> <br /> - They interact with and use the mundane world. But much like career criminals they don't tend to fully engage and always need an exit plan. If an IRS probe could cause you problems. You're dead.<br /> <br /> - the statement was in ideal circumstances. In ideal circumstances you are wielding artifacts of power that wreck armies and make you untouchable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-16T13:10:08-07:00","id":1305325,"title":"","content":"Guns aren't that good in the system (or reality). You want a minimum of 18 damage dice to average one-shot kills.... which requires some combination of high stats, advantageous situational modifiers, and high powered guns. A cop with Dex 3/Firearms 3 and a heavy pistol would have to roll obnoxiously lucky to one-shot kill someone.<br /> <br /> And for all the casual talk of tossing magic around, it isn't hard to have magic to make yourself not squishy, deflect/avoid a big alpha strike, and counter attack. It's even easier with good mundane combat skills. The system isn't built for epic one-on-one duels, but that's different from close combat fights.<br /> <br /> Prime 2 could be used to boost your knife too... but I'm not sure why we're retreading this idea. Weapons &gt; no weapons. Magic boosts both roughly evenly.<br /> <br /> The idea that mages have to operate like career criminals is silly for one big reason: you don't magic for money. You can keep your mundane activities and your magical activities completely separate. I have a mage that's a business owner... and IRS probe means nothing to him besides annoying paperwork because his business - while very in line with his Focus - isn't part of a Chantry, or his Sanctum or anything like that. It's a shop he owns because it makes him part of the community and money is nice. His exit plan is... he could live without it if he hand to, so anyone messing with it is doing far more harm to his completely mundane employees, and his regular patrons that hang out there, than they'd do to him. Some mages are the way you're describing, some aren't. Mages are hard to generalize about for some reason.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-16T17:45:13-07:00","id":1305359,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1302365-do-you-ever-buy-melee-as-a-mage?p=1305325#post1305325\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Guns aren't that good in the system (or reality). You want a minimum of 18 damage dice to average one-shot kills.... which requires some combination of high stats, advantageous situational modifiers, and high powered guns. A cop with Dex 3/Firearms 3 and a heavy pistol would have to roll obnoxiously lucky to one-shot kill someone.<br /> <br /> And for all the casual talk of tossing magic around, it isn't hard to have magic to make yourself not squishy, deflect/avoid a big alpha strike, and counter attack. It's even easier with good mundane combat skills. The system isn't built for epic one-on-one duels, but that's different from close combat fights.<br /> <br /> Prime 2 could be used to boost your knife too... but I'm not sure why we're retreading this idea. Weapons &gt; no weapons. Magic boosts both roughly evenly.<br /> <br /> The idea that mages have to operate like career criminals is silly for one big reason: you don't magic for money. You can keep your mundane activities and your magical activities completely separate. I have a mage that's a business owner... and IRS probe means nothing to him besides annoying paperwork because his business - while very in line with his Focus - isn't part of a Chantry, or his Sanctum or anything like that. It's a shop he owns because it makes him part of the community and money is nice. His exit plan is... he could live without it if he hand to, so anyone messing with it is doing far more harm to his completely mundane employees, and his regular patrons that hang out there, than they'd do to him. Some mages are the way you're describing, some aren't. Mages are hard to generalize about for some reason.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Your post made me think. Does being a mage, depending on the Tradition, means you have to leave your job/family? I remember the OoH book saying that the hermetic training and mindset makes the mage live for it. I don't remember if this is just about the apprentice time or being full member as well.<br /> I believe Akashics might struggle too.<br /> <br /> Of course, there are some traditions which the mage's job is part of the training, like the scientist etherites. But considering that your job is not part of the tradition activities (like most mystics), this means a mage can't have a family and job??","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-16T18:27:15-07:00","id":1305367,"title":"","content":"There's certainly a possibility of having to cut ties as a mage awakens and needs training away from people that don't understand.<br /> <br /> The Chorus, Dreamspeakers, and Verbena philosophies would all balk at the idea in general. All three are highly invested on a paradigm level of community being part of magic.<br /> <br /> The Cult and Chakravanti are more willing to cut ties as necessary, but both highly value maintaining ties as much as possible. The Euthanatos esp. have this as one of their rules because it helps keep their mages grounded and free of Jhor.<br /> <br /> The Virtual Adepts and Society of Ether are mixed. They don't have a specific philosophy around it, but it's highly likely for them to pursue their studies away from traditional community ties, and focus on their specialist communities instead.<br /> <br /> The Order and the Akashayana are the two that actively encourage mages to seek detachment. The Hermetics want you to master your will, and family/jobs are distractions from that, while the Brotherhood seeings being strong emotional attachments as a detriment to enlightenment. Though the Hermetics are less concerned after you finish your apprenticeship and are fre to grow as you see fit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-16T22:23:35-07:00","id":1305406,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1302365-do-you-ever-buy-melee-as-a-mage?p=1305367#post1305367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Order and the Akashayana are the two that actively encourage mages to seek detachment. The Hermetics want you to master your will, and family/jobs are distractions from that, while the Brotherhood seeings being strong emotional attachments as a detriment to enlightenment. Though the Hermetics are less concerned after you finish your apprenticeship and are fre to grow as you see fit.</div> </div> </div> </div>If I recall right (as written in my post), the Order of Hermes actually quite formally ends a character's 'Oldlife', akin to how the Technocracy does it. The person officially 'dies' or disappears, changing their name and everything. I think there's even a short-story in Truth Beyond Paradox that pretty much has that as a topic.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-17T00:44:25-07:00","id":1305414,"title":"","content":"I was phrasing that more as the Order doesn't really care if you decide to have a mundane life after that.<br /> <br /> Though how literal, and how much the death of the old life is even followed, is something that the books have taken different stances on over the years (and different Houses and all that). For some it's more ritualistic, rather than practical (esp. when you consider that some Hermetics highly prize having children that also join if they also Awaken, which would be hard to do with a death of your old life and all).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-17T07:07:03-07:00","id":1305460,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1302365-do-you-ever-buy-melee-as-a-mage?p=1305414#post1305414\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For some it's more ritualistic, rather than practical (esp. when you consider that some Hermetics highly prize having children that also join if they also Awaken, which would be hard to do with a death of your old life and all).</div> </div> </div> </div>Or, you know, those children could join either way. The Order of Hermes teaches High Sorcery as a matter of course, regardless of whether the apprentice is or ever will be Awakened. Only focusing on the Awakened is a suckers game, and the Order of Hermes is too old and has been burned too much (sometimes literally) to casually let itself be played for a sucker. Not again. (Events like the Second Massasa War notwithstanding).<br /> <br /> It's also worth remembering that the Order of Hermes is far from a uniform entity. They have a dozen Houses, each with its own interpretation of Hermetic theory, their own role to play in the larger Order, and their own House cultures. A House Flambeau mage might feel it best to leave the Oldlife behind (if for no other reason than because Flambeau's rate of turnover has historically been frighteningly high). But a House Fortunae or House Quasitor mage may consider it counter-productive to leave normal life behind. Many of those have day jobs in business or law, and people tend to pay attention if those sorts just show up out of nowhere with no traceable past. Indeed, if you're a public prosecutor or the executive of a financial firm, people tend to go digging for your origins sooner or later, if having a concrete mundane papertrail isn't prerequisite to getting hired in the first place. How do you expect to get hired if you have no high school diploma, let alone a university degree or personal/professional references?<br /> <br /> And the Order of Hermes needs people in those positions in mundane society. Long gone are the days when a wizard could just transmute lead into gold and pay the bills that way; the Syndicate pay too much attention for that to work, except in sporadic instances. These ties also allow Hermetics to influence those areas of society, or at least keep abreast of them. Further, while no one could condemn a wizard for spending decades in their Sanctum, reading and experimenting, that sort of thing doesn't push back the tide of Disbelief that keeps Hermetic Arts out of the Consensus. One must be IN the outside world, in order to influence popular opinion and affect institutions in a manner favorable to the Order and the Tradition Council at large. Nor can cloistered magi who retreat from the world have a say in whether the Technocracy use their own hold on institutions to make life harder for traditionalists.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}